1
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:13,267
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:15,485 --> 00:00:20,287
You know what I like about being hopelessly
trapped HERE compared to other places?

3
00:00:20,287 --> 00:00:22,519
I'm not going to immediately die.

4
00:00:22,519 --> 00:00:26,466
That room that was underwater? I
was going to run out of air in MINUTES,

5
00:00:26,466 --> 00:00:29,549
or being pinned down by
artillery fire. Jesus!

6
00:00:29,549 --> 00:00:31,611
This is downright peaceful.

7
00:00:31,611 --> 00:00:33,601
STILL WANT TO GET OUT, THOUGH!

8
00:00:34,259 --> 00:00:35,200
What the f...?

9
00:00:37,293 --> 00:00:38,767
So, how did THAT happen?

10
00:00:39,483 --> 00:00:40,801
Was it a ghost?

11
00:00:41,926 --> 00:00:42,634
Wooo-ooo-oo!

12
00:00:46,372 --> 00:00:48,033
I'm a ghost! Wooooo!

13
00:00:49,779 --> 00:00:51,381
I'm a ghost with a shotgun!

14
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:56,567
I'm going to haunt... the shit out of you!

15
00:00:57,274 --> 00:01:00,180
Okay, so, seriously,
what the hell happened?

16
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:03,218
Did a ghost let me out of that pipe?

17
00:01:03,218 --> 00:01:05,191
Let's examine the evidence.

18
00:01:05,191 --> 00:01:08,051
That hatch was sealed shut when it opened.

19
00:01:08,051 --> 00:01:12,278
I saw nobody there, so either
one of the soldiers unlocked it,

20
00:01:12,278 --> 00:01:16,469
then sprinted away around the
corner and then turned his back to me,

21
00:01:16,469 --> 00:01:17,851
or else it was a ghost.

22
00:01:17,851 --> 00:01:23,342
I suppose it could've been a time-delayed
opening like a bank vault, but wow,

23
00:01:23,342 --> 00:01:25,062
I really doubt that.

24
00:01:25,062 --> 00:01:31,043
No, I think a ghost just let me out of
there like Jack Torrance in "The Shining".

25
00:01:31,043 --> 00:01:32,376
Where am I going?

26
00:01:32,376 --> 00:01:37,000
So, a ghost let me out. Does that mean
I have to kill people now, or... wait.

27
00:01:37,854 --> 00:01:39,421
Oh, there's another pipe.

28
00:01:39,421 --> 00:01:43,659
Yeah, why not? I won't get stuck.
The ghosts have my back now.

29
00:01:43,659 --> 00:01:45,167
Wish they'd showed up sooner.

30
00:01:45,806 --> 00:01:51,431
Yeah, look at this hatch. There is NO WAY
something like this opens up by accident.

31
00:01:51,431 --> 00:01:54,812
So, it's confirmed: I've been
chosen by ghosts.

32
00:01:54,812 --> 00:01:57,743
Well, in "The Shining", they let
him out so he could kill his family,

33
00:01:57,743 --> 00:01:59,572
but that doesn't really apply to me.

34
00:01:59,572 --> 00:02:01,805
Maybe I've been looking at this
the wrong way.

35
00:02:01,805 --> 00:02:04,564
I'm doing the world a FAVOR by
killing these people,

36
00:02:04,564 --> 00:02:07,829
because I'm stopping their
horrible timelines from continuing.

37
00:02:07,829 --> 00:02:09,167
I don't know...

38
00:02:09,167 --> 00:02:12,367
I mean, the ghosts haven't been especially
clear with me what their message is,

39
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:15,634
so if I get confused and kill a bunch of
people, am I really to blame?

40
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:17,146
Y'know...

41
00:02:17,146 --> 00:02:18,572
HECU: Go! Is that all you got?!

42
00:02:18,572 --> 00:02:19,734
...I don't think I am.

43
00:02:23,556 --> 00:02:27,655
And I'm not hearing any contrary
opinions, so I guess it's unanimous.

44
00:02:27,655 --> 00:02:31,711
Okay, so if I have ghosts watching me,
I have to be careful not to get too cocky,

45
00:02:31,711 --> 00:02:34,411
because they like to get your
back and then just drop you.

46
00:02:34,411 --> 00:02:36,490
[lock jiggles]
Wait, I'm not a ghost, am I?

47
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:37,913
No.

48
00:02:37,913 --> 00:02:39,979
Okay, let's all stay
on the same page here.

49
00:02:39,979 --> 00:02:44,303
Now, what I could REALLY use from the
ghosts is for them to leave me some car keys,

50
00:02:44,303 --> 00:02:45,105
and the car...

51
00:02:45,105 --> 00:02:46,500
GUARD: Stand back!
WUAAAAH!

52
00:02:47,371 --> 00:02:48,278
GUARD: Hello.
Okay...

53
00:02:48,278 --> 00:02:50,422
the ghosts aren't telling me to kill you,

54
00:02:50,422 --> 00:02:53,256
so I guess you get to join
the Freeman Fan Club.

55
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:56,302
GUARD: Okay, why not? Didn't
want to die alone anyway.

56
00:02:56,302 --> 00:02:59,779
Oh, you're not going to die
ALONE, don't worry about that.

57
00:02:59,779 --> 00:03:01,140
We have that problem covered.

58
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:04,538
GUARD: Man, I'd like to get my hands
on the guy responsible for THIS mess.

59
00:03:04,538 --> 00:03:08,149
Oh, and don't be discouraged by the
fact that everyone who HAS followed me

60
00:03:08,149 --> 00:03:11,854
is dead or stranded right now,
because that's mostly not my fault.

61
00:03:11,854 --> 00:03:15,464
In the rare event it WAS my
fault--yeah, go and open that--

62
00:03:15,464 --> 00:03:17,907
it still wasn't REALLY my fault.

63
00:03:17,907 --> 00:03:23,466
See, the thing is, I have high standards
and a lot of people don't live up to them.

64
00:03:23,466 --> 00:03:28,988
And, for some reason, many people don't
believe me when I say we need to do something

65
00:03:28,988 --> 00:03:31,321
and end up facing the consequences.

66
00:03:31,321 --> 00:03:35,342
What I'm saying here is, people
who don't listen to me tend to die, alright?

67
00:03:35,342 --> 00:03:38,099
GUARD: Yep, all that target
range time is going to pay off today.

68
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:40,118
Okay, shut up, we've
gone in circles again.

69
00:03:40,118 --> 00:03:41,627
[vortigaunts charge up]

70
00:03:41,627 --> 00:03:42,232
[vortigaunt bolt]

71
00:03:42,232 --> 00:03:45,701
Okay, there are sandbags right
fucking here. Do you see this?

72
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:47,267
Nope.

73
00:03:50,921 --> 00:03:52,642
I am not impressed, man.

74
00:03:52,642 --> 00:03:56,538
GUARD: Sorry, sir... but... I
can't take much more of this.

75
00:03:56,538 --> 00:03:59,415
Okay, we are NOT off to a good start here.

76
00:03:59,415 --> 00:04:00,875
First, you lead me in circles,

77
00:04:00,875 --> 00:04:04,037
now you're complaining your feet
hurt after two minutes of walking.

78
00:04:04,037 --> 00:04:06,463
Is this what is called
"learned helplessness"?

79
00:04:06,463 --> 00:04:07,784
I've heard of that before.

80
00:04:07,784 --> 00:04:09,500
Oh, and don't walk on this thing.

81
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:13,358
Not that you're going to do anything
I say, but... yeah, you're going die,

82
00:04:13,358 --> 00:04:14,901
I can see that right now.

83
00:04:16,601 --> 00:04:18,361
Oh, you know the code!

84
00:04:18,361 --> 00:04:23,069
That's great. Your death will go
towards a greater good.

85
00:04:23,069 --> 00:04:24,519
Y'know, me.

86
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:28,062
Now, don't expect a statue or
anything, unless you make it yourself,

87
00:04:28,062 --> 00:04:30,599
but with all the bombing,
there's not really much point.

88
00:04:30,599 --> 00:04:31,177
[pounding]

89
00:04:31,177 --> 00:04:32,734
[gunshots]
Oh, boy! This is the wrong way!

90
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,787
NOW'S YOUR CHANCE! SHOOT HIM!

91
00:04:35,787 --> 00:04:36,894
YOU SHOOT HIS ASS!

92
00:04:36,894 --> 00:04:38,735
[car alarm]
GOOD! FUCKING DO IT!

93
00:04:38,735 --> 00:04:43,618
[panting]

94
00:04:43,618 --> 00:04:46,327
[gargantua roars]
[panting]

95
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:47,425
Another gate...

96
00:04:47,425 --> 00:04:51,507
I don't think I can smash through this
one even though I have a running start.

97
00:04:51,507 --> 00:04:53,885
Okay, time for the asphalt tumor ride.

98
00:04:53,885 --> 00:04:56,434
It's not working--WAAAAAHHHH!

99
00:04:57,968 --> 00:04:59,834
WUAAAH-WAAAAH-AAAAAH!

100
00:05:00,457 --> 00:05:01,868
That worked out okay...

101
00:05:03,603 --> 00:05:05,273
Is someone following me?

102
00:05:05,273 --> 00:05:07,968
Oh, it's dead man walking. Bye!

103
00:05:08,385 --> 00:05:09,367
Waaaah!

104
00:05:10,662 --> 00:05:12,769
RADIO: Come in, Cooper. Do you copy?

105
00:05:12,769 --> 00:05:13,542
Sir, yes sir!

106
00:05:13,542 --> 00:05:16,784
RADIO: Forget about Freeman!
We're abandoning the base.

107
00:05:16,784 --> 00:05:18,918
RADIO: If you have any last bomb targets,

108
00:05:18,918 --> 00:05:20,604
What does this do?
RADIO: mark them tactical map.

109
00:05:20,604 --> 00:05:22,889
[plane whine]
RADIO: Otherwise, get the hell out of there!

110
00:05:22,889 --> 00:05:23,918
[explosions]
RADIO: Otherwise, get the hell out of there!

111
00:05:23,918 --> 00:05:25,709
Oh!
RADIO: Repeat, we are pulling out

112
00:05:25,709 --> 00:05:27,574
RADIO: and commencing airstrikes.

113
00:05:27,574 --> 00:05:29,802
RADIO: Give us targets or get below!

114
00:05:29,802 --> 00:05:32,934
Oh, I'll give you targets. Does
this do what I think it does?

115
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:36,598
[plane whine]

116
00:05:36,598 --> 00:05:38,553
[explosions]

117
00:05:38,553 --> 00:05:41,394
Amazing! I didn't even see the plane.

118
00:05:41,394 --> 00:05:42,812
[rumbling]

119
00:05:42,812 --> 00:05:44,584
Uh-oh. Maybe I shouldn't have done that.

120
00:05:44,584 --> 00:05:46,677
[pounding]

121
00:05:46,677 --> 00:05:49,120
Oh, shit, that buckled fast.

122
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,481
Uh, yeah, let's do it again.

123
00:05:50,481 --> 00:05:52,173
[plane whine]

124
00:05:52,173 --> 00:05:53,525
[explosions]
Yes, walk into it!

125
00:05:53,525 --> 00:05:57,968
Good Godzilla! THAT'S A GOOD
GODZILLA! YES, THAT'S A GOOD JOB!

126
00:05:58,846 --> 00:06:04,096
Wow. Lucky that thing doesn't have
a fear response. Most animals have that.

127
00:06:04,096 --> 00:06:08,148
I guess the thought something
kicking its ass just confuses it.

128
00:06:08,148 --> 00:06:09,887
So, let's bomb something else.

129
00:06:09,887 --> 00:06:12,734
I've got time for this. I'll make time.

130
00:06:15,204 --> 00:06:16,145
That looks good...

131
00:06:16,145 --> 00:06:18,169
[plane whine]
I guess...

132
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:21,245
[explosions]

133
00:06:21,245 --> 00:06:23,322
Oh, man, nothing.

134
00:06:23,322 --> 00:06:25,875
That must be SERIOUSLY reinforced,

135
00:06:25,875 --> 00:06:29,581
like those rubber alloy walls
they use on nuclear reactors.

136
00:06:29,581 --> 00:06:32,087
Well, let's try and take out
that radio tower.

137
00:06:32,087 --> 00:06:37,150
I think LESS communication is
BEST communication.

138
00:06:37,150 --> 00:06:38,144
Yeah, there we go.

139
00:06:38,144 --> 00:06:40,547
[plane whine]

140
00:06:40,547 --> 00:06:43,167
[explosions]

141
00:06:43,167 --> 00:06:45,081
Nothing again?

142
00:06:45,081 --> 00:06:47,511
These are some surgical strikes!

143
00:06:47,511 --> 00:06:49,870
[plane whine]
I actually am pretty amazed

144
00:06:49,870 --> 00:06:51,255
[plane whine]
at the accuracy of these pilots.

145
00:06:51,255 --> 00:06:54,176
[explosions]
Ohhh! Yeah!

146
00:06:54,176 --> 00:06:56,308
Yeah, that's more like it.

147
00:06:56,308 --> 00:06:59,069
Now we're cooking with Composition H6.

148
00:06:59,069 --> 00:07:00,980
This is going to solve my problems.

149
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:05,165
When all you have is aerial strike map,
everything looks like a bomb target.

150
00:07:05,165 --> 00:07:06,507
[plane whine]
Where's the plane?

151
00:07:06,507 --> 00:07:07,802
[explosions]

152
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:10,807
Oh, yeah, I could get used to this.

153
00:07:10,807 --> 00:07:15,714
I am again surprised there's no
authentication here; just two big joysticks

154
00:07:15,714 --> 00:07:16,744
and a red button.
[plane whine]

155
00:07:16,744 --> 00:07:18,334
[plane whine]

156
00:07:18,334 --> 00:07:20,291
[explosions]

157
00:07:20,291 --> 00:07:22,537
I guess the military
understood the intelligence

158
00:07:22,537 --> 00:07:24,550
of the people they were working with.

159
00:07:24,550 --> 00:07:27,041
And that gate is still standing.

160
00:07:27,041 --> 00:07:30,085
Actually, why does this place
have a moat to begin with?

161
00:07:30,085 --> 00:07:32,063
[plane whine]

162
00:07:32,063 --> 00:07:32,869
[explosions]

163
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:35,323
Ahahahaha!

164
00:07:35,323 --> 00:07:38,943
You know, this map is great,
but it has one severe flaw

165
00:07:38,943 --> 00:07:41,112
and that it's too small.

166
00:07:41,112 --> 00:07:43,195
I need one of the whole world.

167
00:07:43,195 --> 00:07:47,295
I can't bring it with me so I guess I'll
just keep heading to greener pastures.

168
00:07:47,295 --> 00:07:50,982
Although my "green pastures" are
more like sunbaked badlands

169
00:07:50,982 --> 00:07:53,633
covered with bodies and alien growths.

170
00:07:53,633 --> 00:07:54,725
And mines.

171
00:07:54,725 --> 00:07:56,325
And people shooting at me.

172
00:07:56,325 --> 00:08:00,983
I really do like, however, how that
officer said, "Forget about Freeman."

173
00:08:00,983 --> 00:08:04,592
I still think it's psychotic
they've made me a priority,

174
00:08:04,592 --> 00:08:06,412
but calling it off is good.

175
00:08:06,412 --> 00:08:10,149
I just hope I'm not the only
person who received those orders,

176
00:08:10,149 --> 00:08:12,400
because that would just be redundant.

177
00:08:12,922 --> 00:08:14,326
[plane whine]

178
00:08:14,326 --> 00:08:16,275
[explosions]
Uh, I didn't call this one in--

179
00:08:16,275 --> 00:08:17,300
Yeah, I'm going to leave.

180
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:18,662
[plane whine, explosions]

181
00:08:18,663 --> 00:08:21,347
I'm starting to get that feeling
again like I don't belong here,

182
00:08:21,347 --> 00:08:22,260
[plane whine]
and the irony is,

183
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:23,537
[explosions]
I don't even want to be here.

184
00:08:23,537 --> 00:08:24,869
So, you think, I don't want to be here,

185
00:08:24,869 --> 00:08:26,162
[plane whine]
they don't want me here,

186
00:08:26,162 --> 00:08:28,386
[explosions]
this problem should solve itself pretty rapidly,

187
00:08:28,386 --> 00:08:30,345
[plane whine]
but it really seems to be persisting

188
00:08:30,345 --> 00:08:31,318
[plane whine]
quite aggressively.

189
00:08:31,318 --> 00:08:36,015
[plane whine, explosions]
Oh! We are not deep enough yet, are we?

190
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:38,234
[explosions]
WAAAAH! HOLY SHIT!

191
00:08:39,099 --> 00:08:40,519
[plane whine]
Oh, yeah! Go dark!

192
00:08:40,519 --> 00:08:43,593
[plane whine]
That would make everything... perfect right now...

193
00:08:43,593 --> 00:08:47,243
[explosions]
If I couldn't see in the middle of all this, that would--

194
00:08:47,243 --> 00:08:47,707
[screaming]

195
00:08:47,707 --> 00:08:48,995
[plane whine]

196
00:08:48,995 --> 00:08:50,082
[explosions]

197
00:08:50,082 --> 00:08:51,628
[screaming]

198
00:08:51,628 --> 00:08:55,261
Don't crush me--THIS SUIT DOESN'T DO
SHIT AGAINST 50 TONS OF ROCK!

199
00:08:55,261 --> 00:08:57,097
[explosions]

200
00:08:57,097 --> 00:08:58,694
Is that gas filling the room?

201
00:08:58,694 --> 00:09:01,554
I don't know how I feel about
that with those sparks up there.

202
00:09:01,554 --> 00:09:03,667
No, I DO know how I feel about that!

203
00:09:04,713 --> 00:09:07,601
See, this is why I like the pipe.

204
00:09:10,665 --> 00:09:13,367
Uh, ghosts? Any time now...

205
00:09:13,916 --> 00:09:18,467
[distant explosions]

